+(duration)=
+
+### Duration
+
+The {class}`Duration` type converts a length of time to a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. The value is either a whole
+number of seconds, such as `120`, or one or more `<integer><unit>` groups using the units `d` (days), `h` (hours),
+`m` (minutes), and `s` (seconds), such as `2d`, `1h30m`, `45s`, or `1d2h3m4s`. Each unit may be given at most once and
+in that order, without spaces. Units are case-insensitive. Anything else, such as negative or decimal numbers, fails
+with an error.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="1h30m", show_default=True)
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"Waiting for {timeout}.")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=90'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=2d'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h 30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--help'])
+```
+
+```{versionadded} 8.5.1
+```
+
